cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Shared readouts, not S³: what drives forgetting in a toy quaternion network"
abstract: >-
  A controlled study of catastrophic forgetting in small quaternion networks,
  with a pilot on real images. In a toy problem, forgetting comes mostly from
  reading tasks out of one shared output quaternion, not from constraining
  weights to the unit sphere (S³); a further S³ cost from the amplitude ×
  unit-quaternion factorization did not transfer to split digits. On split
  digits, quaternion layers with per-task outputs forget less than real MLPs
  of the same size. Includes reproducible JavaScript and Python engines, raw
  results and an interactive browser workbench.
